      "statement": "A LangSmith missing-box response is classified as `SandboxGoneError` and can be recreated, whereas other reconnection failures become `SandboxUnreachableError` and normally are not replaced because replacement loses uncommitted working-tree state; reviewer callers explicitly allow replacement because they re-derive their checkout.",
